{
  "about": "The labelled phrase set: spoken-style phrases with the intent and slots they must give, through vcd's own routing (the fast grammar, then the brain with the catalogue). kind: fast (the fast grammar must match it, with exactly these slots), intent (the brain must call these tools), talk (no action at all), grounded (no action; the answer must say a fact from the context line), unknown (no action; the answer must say it doesn't know, and must not state the fact: the small model never answers from its own knowledge). Slots: a value matches when equal (words compared without case or punctuation, numbers as numbers); \"~x\" when it contains x; a list when any matches; \"*\" when present. An intent name \"a|b\" accepts either.",
